                <pb facs="0998" n="904" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg904"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 856.—Telegram—Received April 9,
                        1896.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Riddle.</hi></head>
                <p>Remind Grand Vizier of his assurance that the pledges of the race of old Turks
                    could be relied on, and tell him I have assured the Government of the United
                    States that his promise that Knapp should remain undisturbed at Bitlis until
                    last of April would be observed. <pb facs="0999" n="905" xml:id="pg905"/> Unless
                    sensational news about missionary danger ceases and Knapp returns at once to
                    Bitlis and remains there until you send for him I will instantly [return] to my
                    post. Answer at once to Secretary of State.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
